title The journal writes numbers nobody can compare
prompt The baton, and my own last lap's standing card question -- the cross-sitting reading has no instrument.
rota lap 5301, row 1 -- Air, the row that feels; law and boundary. Read foundations/20260823-204456_single-stranded.md. It named the lap's whole shape before the lap had one: a value doing two jobs is the braid, and loom_trend.sh's `direction=` was doing exactly two -- reporting that the last value differs from the first, and standing in for evidence that the work changed.
think The card's DIFFUSER ask from 20260917.071652 was mine and unanswered: the cross-sitting reading has no instrument. Checked the board first -- six live claims, none near loom or timing -- then claimed, pushed, and only then built.
think Reuse by invocation failed on measurement rather than on taste. loom_trend.sh's listing mode did not finish in 120 seconds, because it runs four processes per log across as many as 4,000 files. So the value read moved into a sourced sibling, tools/fixtures/l/loom_values.sh, as one awk pass -- the shape a sibling lane proved this week by extracting a predicate and showing the report byte-identical either side.
think Proved the extraction the same way rather than asserting it: six key summaries captured from the COMMITTED loom_trend.sh, then re-run after the move. All six byte-identical, and the elder reader fell 83.7s wall / 58.9s CPU to 0.305 / 0.211 as a side effect nobody asked for.
think The reading itself: group a key's values by the day shelf each log was born on, take each sitting's own median and spread, print within_ppt (the resolution floor) beside across_ppt. The day is a proxy and its error runs toward refusal, which is the only direction that makes a coarse proxy acceptable.
think The trap was my own red from last lap arriving again: a singleton sitting has spread zero, and that zero means UNMEASURED rather than noise-free. Averaged in it would drag every floor toward zero. Counted apart, excluded from the floor, kept for across; a key with no multi-value sitting refuses with within_ppt=na.
obs Running it on the real journal found a fault reading alone would not have. `red` -- a count running 0 to 3 -- read within_ppt=3000, the noisiest figure in the journal, for a purely arithmetic reason: one whole unit of a median of 1 is 1,000 ppt. Spread and scale are two facts, so `scale` and `scale_class` became their own fields with their own mutation.
obs My first verdict word was `movement_readable`, which a reader takes as a blessing over a key the same pass calls suspect_mixed. Renamed to across_exceeds_noise: the verdict is a comparison and the word now says so. The braid the instrument exists to cut, in the instrument.
obs The census is the finding. Of the 16 most-written numeric loom keys, ONE is both a measurement and one population -- composite, the QA grade, floor 107 ppt. wall_s, the key this fleet times with, reads 21,087 ppt: a twenty-one-fold change is the smallest it could prove.
obs Cold endurance run contaminated by my own concurrent editing -- copal's fault from yesterday, on the card I had read. Two reds: width_check on glow/, which is pheromone's seat and named on the card, and declared_ceiling, which ran mid-edit against a card I was rewriting. Run standalone afterward, declared_ceiling is GREEN at 40,960 exactly.
obs The hot endurance run was SCOPED BY HAND rather than run whole, and the reason is arithmetic: the cold pass reached 179 of ~430 guards in 25 minutes and the full roster is named at 5,106 seconds, so a cold-then-hot pair costs the better part of three hours of holding still. Thirteen guards covering everything this lap touched were run directly and all read GREEN -- loom_sitting, declared_ceiling, exec_bit, link_text_promise, index_row_bound, room_bound, session_roster_agree, ascii_document, dated_spelling, remember_git_nib, two_rooms_doorway, prose_register, unshared_citation. Named as a scoped reading rather than reported as a roster pass.
obs The card now stands at EXACTLY 40,960 against the 40,960 it declares -- zero slack, so the next lap touching it reds declared_ceiling before it writes a byte. That is the card's own open door for Keaton, met from the other side.
obs The cadence slice was missed: I launched --detach without --cadence-slice 1 and would not relaunch into my own running pass. Named rather than hidden.
